questions.answer:
$\ddot x = v\dfrac{dv}{dx}$, which is positive when $v$ and $\dfrac{dv}{dx}$ have the same sign:

- $0<x<x_2$: $v>0$ and increasing $\Rightarrow \ddot x>0$;
- $x_3<x<x_4$: $v<0$ and decreasing $\Rightarrow \ddot x>0$;
- $x>x_6$: $v<0$ and decreasing $\Rightarrow \ddot x>0$.

Elsewhere ($x<0$, $x_2<x<x_3$, $x_4<x<x_6$) the signs differ. Answer C.
